we're going to talk about,

00:01:00.301 --> 00:01:02.480
we're going to talk
about your perspectives.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.130
- And we do this, we do
this on Twitter, you know.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.483
- Twitter, @mythical.

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:08.930
Follow us.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.490
- Some people have
created Twitter accounts

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.400
just to participate.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.850
We appreciate that.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:13.683
- That's not--

00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:14.910
- We hear you, we notice.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:16.970
So we'll get to that in a second,

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:20.835
but something has happened
to me two days in a row.

00:01:20.835 --> 00:01:23.287
And I just want to throw it out there

00:01:23.287 --> 00:01:26.800
and see if you think there's
any significance to it.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.013
- Oh, significance.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.033
Okay.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:30.930
- This is not unusual.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.500
I think that lots of people
talk about this phenomenon

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.750
but it hasn't happened to me

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:39.150
in a while and it's
happened two days in a row.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:39.983
- Okay.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.486
- Waking up and knowing

00:01:45.486 --> 00:01:50.000
that I have woken up one minute
before my alarm goes off.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.360
- Oh, yes, yeah, yeah.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.280
- And not just, not just looking--

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.113
- It's uncanny.

00:01:55.113 --> 00:01:58.280
- Not just looking over to guess,

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.550
but having a knowledge and then
looking over to confirm it.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.890
- Oh, okay.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.130
So you have a knowledge, okay?

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.780
Your eyes aren't even open yet,

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.700
but you know you're waking up

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.920
and you're about to look at the clock

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.710
and you're saying, my
clock is going to go off

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.470
in one minute, you know that.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:21.270
- Well, so my phone is on a
little stand, a wireless stand.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.040
Not, it's not something
that, I can live without it.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.970
It's not an item that
I'm going to talk about,

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:29.090
but it is a new thing that
I got that has my watch,

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:33.450
my phone and my air, what
do you call them, AirPods?

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.580
- I don't know.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.440
- All wirelessly charging on one thing.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.610
It was kind of cool, but
my phone, here's why I know

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:44.300
that I'm not being
influenced by seeing it.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.070
I have to hit my phone

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:48.710
in order to turn the screen
on, to see what time it is.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.300
That's the only indication
of what time it is.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.970
So yesterday I woke up.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:52.803
- It's interesting.

00:02:52.803 --> 00:02:54.930
- I was like, my alarm is about to go off.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:56.280
Like, literally, it's going to go off

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.620
if I don't reach over there,
reach over there, 6:29.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:03.030
My alarm went off at 6:30,

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.510
but I stopped it
literally like 15 seconds.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.000
So I was like, oh,
okay, well that happens.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.093
This morning, alarm is set for 6:15.

00:03:12.976 --> 00:03:15.189
I don't get up at the same time every day.

00:03:15.189 --> 00:03:17.519
Had different things going on.

00:03:17.519 --> 00:03:19.660
That's the weird thing.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.748
- Oh, two different time.

00:03:20.748 --> 00:03:21.590
Okay.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.900
That kind of blows the theory here.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.860
- Right, that's why I'm so shaken by it.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.120
- That's crazy.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.500
So today was day two, this morning?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.640
I got to get more data man 'cause--

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.601
- Okay, I woke up this morning
and I had the same feeling

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:39.601
and I will say just in full
disclosure, it was 6:13.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.060
So it wasn't 6:14, it wasn't one minute,

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.700
but it was two minutes.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.700
And I was like, and I was like--

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.840
- So it was the second day in a row,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.650
and you wouldn't set it at the same time.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.336
- I did it again, here's the thing.

00:03:49.336 --> 00:03:50.622
This isn't normal.

00:03:50.622 --> 00:03:54.150
Now, when I get up at the same time,

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.590
but I don't get up at the same time.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.423
I don't--

00:03:56.423 --> 00:03:59.510
- I get up at the same
time and there's many times

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.820
when I wake up right
before the alarm goes off.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.640
- But you also go to bed
at the same time, right?

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.473
- Yeah.

00:04:05.473 --> 00:04:06.306
- You go to bed at the same time

00:04:06.306 --> 00:04:07.139
and you get up at the same time.

00:04:07.139 --> 00:04:08.960
This is not unusual.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.739
But I haven't gone to
bed at the same time--

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:11.927
- I'd like to think I was special too so.

00:04:11.927 --> 00:04:14.910
- No, because your body
adjusts to a rhythm.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.010
- No, I'm special.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.610
- You're special in other
ways, everyone knows that.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.253
But I don't go to bed at
the same time every day.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:26.873
My bed time range is--

00:04:26.873 --> 00:04:28.909
- It's not a circadian thing.

00:04:28.909 --> 00:04:30.380
- I mean sometimes I might be like,

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.320
I'm really tired and
I'll go to bed at 9:30.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.240
Like I'll go to bed at 9:30

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.710
and then sometimes I'll
be like, it's midnight.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.240
I haven't thought about bed yet.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.430
I'll go to bed at 12:30.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.260
And any of these things can happen.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.110
It has nothing to do,

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.436
it's just whatever happens, happens.

00:04:45.436 --> 00:04:48.240
And then the morning is based
on what I need to do that day.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.640
- So when you're going to
bed, do you make the decision?

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.863
Do you set your alarm clock?

00:04:52.863 --> 00:04:55.850
Because that's changing too apparently.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.230
You make a decision,
is it, will it be 6:15,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.740
will it be 6:30?

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:00.573
- Yeah.

00:05:00.573 --> 00:05:04.863
- And how big of a range is that?

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.303
- No earlier than six o'clock,

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:13.810
no later than 7:30, and if I need to,

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.670
if I want to sleep later,
I can't sleep past 7:30,

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.503
I cannot.

00:05:17.503 --> 00:05:20.270
It is physically, now
that I've hit my 40s,

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.457
physically impossible to sleep past 7:30

00:05:22.457 --> 00:05:24.330
and I really, really hate that.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.940
- I can go back to
sleep, but I do wake up.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.040
Well, listen, I'm going
to count the third day,

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:29.873
this morning.

00:05:29.873 --> 00:05:31.203
You got three days in a row.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:33.950
I think you need to keep tracking this

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.900
because maybe there's some,

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:36.910
this is something to be harnessed.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.650
- Do you think it's supernatural?

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.483
- No.

00:05:39.483 --> 00:05:40.316
- That's really what the question is.

00:05:40.316 --> 00:05:42.390
- I wish it was, that
would be fun to talk about.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:43.223
- Do you think this is--

00:05:43.223 --> 00:05:44.950
- No, but you can't say it's supernatural.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:46.880
- Do you think it's
the beginning of maybe,

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.820
I could be, maybe I'm like,
this is my origin story,

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.063
for like a superhero.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.730
The guy who can wake up
right before his alarm

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:59.130
and harnesses that as a super power.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.056
- The alarm anticipator.

00:06:00.056 --> 00:06:03.980
- That's good, this is what I'm saying,

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:04.813
I would be called the anticipator

00:06:04.813 --> 00:06:07.770
and I'll start anticipating
things right before they happen

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:09.090
and saving people.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:09.923
- Well, okay.

00:06:09.923 --> 00:06:12.870
Like dismantling a bomb?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.129
- No, it has to be things
that are based on a schedule.

00:06:15.129 --> 00:06:15.990
- Like if you were taking a nap?

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.265
- Like if a train was coming.

00:06:17.265 --> 00:06:20.160
- If you were taking a nap,

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.607
and there was a bomb,

00:06:21.607 --> 00:06:25.760
you could maximize your sleep
and then wake up and defuse

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.080
the bomb right before it goes off,

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.808
thereby getting the most rest possible,

00:06:30.808 --> 00:06:32.454
so you have a good day.

00:06:32.454 --> 00:06:33.780
- I think that's too complex.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.780
I think it's more like, there is a child

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:42.720
that has fallen into the
place where the trains come

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:43.943
in the subway.

00:06:43.943 --> 00:06:47.900
- Okay, you're taking a nap
and as the child is falling,

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.870
you wake up right before it
hits the asphalt and catch it.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.260
- No, no, no, again, I wake up
right before the train comes.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.309
I let the child be down there.

00:06:55.309 --> 00:06:56.142
Maybe seven--

00:06:56.142 --> 00:06:57.720
- If the child hit the
ground, it probably died.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.900
- No, no, no, he landed on his
feet and then he rolled over

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.130
and now everyone's panicking,

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:03.370
they're trying like, should we pull him up

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:07.110
and I'm sleeping seven to eight
minutes and then I'm like,

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.307
train's coming and then
I wake up and then I see

00:07:09.307 --> 00:07:11.230
the child, I didn't know about the child,

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.063
I see the child because I've woken up

00:07:12.063 --> 00:07:14.770
because the train is coming,
and then because I got

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:15.810
long arms--

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:16.643
- Okay, I get it.

00:07:16.643 --> 00:07:17.476
- I pull up.

00:07:17.476 --> 00:07:18.810
- So really--

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.208
- Yeah, that's the
superhero that I'm gonna be,

00:07:20.208 --> 00:07:21.041
the anticipator.

00:07:21.041 --> 00:07:23.920
- You're really, and
what that means is that

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.200
you're a superhero with no real powers

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.620
except that you can maximize your sleep

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.860
before doing something
that you need to do.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:33.740
As a matter of fact, you're
kind of like a normal

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.450
person that wakes up with
an alarm and does something.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.860
- I think you're seeing
the wrong end of this

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:39.753
and what I'm saying it has
nothing to do with the sleep.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.430
The sleep is only the
way that the anticipator

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:44.900
begins to anticipate.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.500
So you put the anticipator in a situation

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.750
where something could
be on certain schedule.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:52.925
Like, put the anticipator
in there, put him to sleep,

00:07:52.925 --> 00:07:55.430
he'll wake up right
before this thing happens.

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.087
- But the reason why he's so good--

00:07:57.087 --> 00:07:58.190
- Not to defuse the bomb,

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:00.090
but right before the bomb goes off.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.430
So probably too late,
but at least we'll know

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:03.263
it's gonna happen.

00:08:03.263 --> 00:08:04.720
- Well, you can take that into account,

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.130
you can anticipate the amount of time

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.310
it takes to defuse the bomb

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:08.355
if you're the anticipator.

00:08:08.355 --> 00:08:10.190
- I don't think I can
get that sophisticated.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.083
- Then you suck.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.570
But you're gonna be well-rested,

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.983
and I think that counts for something.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.630
- Yeah.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.940
- It's interesting because just last week

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:25.310
we were talking about
strange habits of successful

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.540
people and one of the things
we didn't talk about was

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.830
there's a number of people that wake up

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:32.913
without an alarm clock, Oprah,

00:08:34.009 --> 00:08:35.620
she's the only one I remember
off the top of my head.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:38.690
- Oprah, the list can stop there,

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.768
and it would be a ringing endorsement.

00:08:40.768 --> 00:08:43.668
- I think after a while,
there's no ringing,

00:08:43.668 --> 00:08:44.813
that's the point.

00:08:46.052 --> 00:08:49.180
It's a silent endorsement of waking up

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.013
without an alarm clock.

00:08:50.013 --> 00:08:51.143
So you could do that.

00:08:51.143 --> 00:08:52.893
- I could do that now.

00:08:52.893 --> 00:08:53.910
- Then that is a--

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.050
- I can't sleep past 7:30.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:56.670
- And here's another thing, by the way--

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:58.640
- But I can say, five
o'clock, don't need an alarm.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:08:59.473
Is that what she does?

00:08:59.473 --> 00:09:01.190
She sets a time and then
just wakes up for it?

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:05.230
- I think I know why this
is happening with you,

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:08.100
because you have
inadvertently set up a system

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.993
to train yourself to do this.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.650
You don't have a clock
that's easily visible

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:18.550
from your bed, you have to
wake up more than you need to

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.910
in order to see what time
it is, to see if you need

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.707
to get up, for me,

00:09:22.707 --> 00:09:26.815
I have a clock visible there,

00:09:26.815 --> 00:09:28.800
I don't use it as the
alarm, I use my phone

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.740
as the wake up alarm,

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.007
but I can just easily roll over

00:09:32.007 --> 00:09:36.270
and just like, kind of, quarter of the way

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:39.250
open one eye, and see what time it is

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.560
and then just immediately
go back to sleep.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.908
That's also why you're
not able to sleep later,

00:09:44.908 --> 00:09:46.580
on the weekends or something,

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:47.850
you just need to be able to roll over

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.730
and give a little crack to the eye,

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.360
oh, I've got 20 minutes, I've got an hour.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.570
- The reason I can't sleep late,

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:56.803
is because, this is a sore
subject between me and my wife,

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:00.700
our bedroom doesn't have blocking blinds,

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.930
because whoever we bought the house from

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:05.450
installed translucent blinds.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.283
- You can change that.

00:10:06.283 --> 00:10:08.383
- This I've been talking about,

00:10:08.383 --> 00:10:11.180
we've been in this house,
for going on six years

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:16.170
and what I told, I tell my wife, you know,

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.120
when we were on tour and
I would be like in a hotel

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.470
with those, you know
there's like vinyl curtains

